# madcide default theme = JOE parity (owner directive 2026-08-26: match
# what joe shows). Mapping observed from joe 4.6's own default scheme
# (/usr/share/joe/colors/default.jcf + syntax/c.jsf class inheritance):
# Comment=green; Constant=cyan (c.jsf: Number and String both inherit
# +Constant); Keyword=bold; Type=bold; idents plain — so `function`
# stays unthemed here (JOE has no function class; our AST-backed one is
# an ADDITION, styled in the vivid/classic schemes). JOE classes we do
# not classify yet (Preproc blue, Brace magenta, Escape bold cyan, Bad
# bold red) are named classifier seats in the JOE look/feel recon doc.
# One class + spec per line (JOE's spec vocabulary; ^K T swaps schemes).
keyword bold
type bold
string cyan
number cyan
comment green
